Vendored Agent Skills
=====================

Skills under `skills_library/` that were vendored from third-party
open-source repositories are listed here with their original license.
Vendoring went through `skills_market`'s install pipeline (content scan,
capability grant, atomic write) — nothing was copied by hand.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
obra/superpowers — MIT License
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source : https://github.com/obra/superpowers (branch `main`, fetched 2026-09-25)
License: MIT (LICENSE file at the repository root)
Copyright (c) 2025 Jesse Vincent

Vendored into `skills_library/software-development/`:

  brainstorming
  dispatching-parallel-agents
  executing-plans
  finishing-a-development-branch
  receiving-code-review
  using-git-worktrees
  verification-before-completion
  writing-plans
  writing-skills

Each was installed granting exactly the one capability it requested
(`files:read`); nothing broader.

Refused by the scanner and therefore NOT vendored:

  subagent-driven-development
    reason: CRITICAL finding `destructive_command` (evidence: `rm -rf`)
            reported against its SKILL.md. The install pipeline is
            fail-closed on blocking findings, so the skill was not
            written to disk. Re-vendoring it requires either an upstream
            change or an explicit decision to grant that capability —
            neither was taken here.

